"""🧚 Punctuation Pixies (English follow-up, 2026-11-01 16:00): PUNCTUATION for every CEFR level. Each card is one sentence
with ONE gap where a mark (or a word with the right capitals, apostrophe or hyphens) goes; the player taps one of 4 tiles.
Punctuation is marked in every Cambridge writing paper and in the editing tasks of the Singapore MOE primary English syllabus,
but the game had no punctuation practice at all.
  A1  full stops · question marks · ! · capital letters (I, names, days, places)          (Starters / P1–P2)
  A2  commas in lists, after Yes/No and before please · short forms (don't, it's, I'll) · capitals for places, months, languages
  B1  possessive apostrophes (Ali's, cats', children's, James's) · speech marks · commas after openers · its / it's
  B2  commas with who/which (extra or needed information, "no mark" = no mark) · colons and semicolons · question tags, reported
      and polite questions, interrupted speech
  C1  dashes and brackets (an aside opens and closes with the same mark) · hyphens in describing words (a ten-year-old, ten years
      old) · semicolons and colons instead of comma splices, semicolons in a list of lists
  C2  commas that change meaning (Let's eat, Grandma! · eats shoots and leaves · However hard) · hyphens that change meaning
      (man-eating, re-signed, re-sort, twenty-odd, coop / co-op) · joint and separate possession, geese's, twins', Whose
Kid- and teen-friendly topics only (picnics, unicorns, markets, holidays, bands, hikes, games, octopuses, the school paper).
  M(sentence with ___, "answer|other right answers", kind, why-tip, "wrong=why not|wrong=why not|wrong=why not")
"no mark" is the tile for "no mark here". A dash answer (—) takes the space after the gap with it (octopus—a master).
kind → the 💡 hint after a first miss (js/marks.js KINDS)."""
from qb import why_tiles
NONE = "no mark"

def M(s, ans, kind, tip, x):
    return {"s": s, "ans": ans.split("|"), "kind": kind, "tip": tip, **why_tiles(x)}

def T(icon, name, focus, items): return {"icon": icon, "name": name, "focus": focus, "items": items}

